1. Learning Rate Warm-up

Instead of starting training with a large learning rate, we start small and gradually increase it.

Why?
It prevents unstable updates at the beginning of training and helps the model learn smoothly.

Simple idea:
Small LR → Gradually increase → Normal LR


2. Transfer Learning

Instead of training a neural network from scratch, we use a pre-trained model that has already learned useful features.

Example:

Pre-trained Model → Reuse learned layers → Train on our dataset

Why?

Requires less data
Faster training
Often gives better performance

Simple idea:

Don't learn everything again; reuse what the model already knows.
